# LF in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Not a style preference: test/smoke.sh and start.sh are run by /bin/sh, and a
# CRLF shebang line makes Linux report "bad interpreter: No such file or
# directory" — naming the interpreter, not the line ending, so it reads as a
# missing shell. Checking these out with CRLF on a Windows box and copying the
# tree to a server reproduces it every time.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touch the runtime binaries. bin/xnet has no extension, so name the
# directory rather than relying on content sniffing.
*.exe  binary
bin/*  binary
